From: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tests: Give the HoloMQ retirement stress test two CUDA queues

cuda_retirement_randomized_stress_test_device and _pinned hold one reader
stream on cuStreamWaitValue32 and wait for the other before checking that the
slot is retained by the gated reader alone, so they assume the two
non-blocking streams run on separate hardware queues. With
CUDA_DEVICE_MAX_CONNECTIONS unset, the Jetson AGX Thor driver behaves as if it
were 1: both streams share a queue and the fast reader cannot finish while the
other is gated. Upstream now detects that and reports the case skipped, which
leaves the retention-by-one-reader path untested on Tegra. With 2, 4, 8 or 32
connections the case runs and passes. Set 8, the documented default, for these
tests only.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
---
diff --git a/tests/holomq/unit/CMakeLists.txt b/tests/holomq/unit/CMakeLists.txt
index 95d2e0efd..02904a91f 100644
--- a/tests/holomq/unit/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/tests/holomq/unit/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -188,8 +188,11 @@ if(NOT cuda_test_sources STREQUAL "")
         add_test(NAME cuda_retirement_randomized_stress_test_${storage}
             COMMAND $<TARGET_FILE:${CUDA_PROJECT_NAME}>
                 "--gtest_filter=*CudaBufferFanoutTest.RandomizedReleaseAndClosingNeverReuseAnUnreadSlot/${parameter}")
+        # The gated reader stream must not share a hardware queue with the other
+        # reader, and Tegra's driver defaults to one queue.
         set_tests_properties(cuda_retirement_randomized_stress_test_${storage} PROPERTIES
-            LABELS "cuda;holomq;stress" TIMEOUT 45 SKIP_REGULAR_EXPRESSION "\\[  SKIPPED \\]")
+            LABELS "cuda;holomq;stress" TIMEOUT 45 SKIP_REGULAR_EXPRESSION "\\[  SKIPPED \\]"
+            ENVIRONMENT "CUDA_DEVICE_MAX_CONNECTIONS=8")
     endforeach()
 
     foreach(cuda_source IN LISTS cuda_test_sources)
